ny45-20P) and U3 (ATtiny13V-10S) are placed with their signal pins on the same nets (POT, PWM, RST, SDA, TACH, +5V, GND).\", \"expected\": \"Two alternative MCUs can share a net list only if they are mutually exclusive (one footprint populated). Both populated would create bus contention on PB0, PB1, PB3, PB4 and the reset line.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U2\\\") (pin \\\"6\\\") (pinfunction \\\"PB1\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U3\\\") (pin \\\"6\\\") (pinfunction \\\"PB1\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\"))\"}], \"impact\": \"If both are fitted, the two MCUs fight over the same pins and reset line, so the fan controller would misbehave or fail to program. If the layout is intentionally one-or-the-other, this is not a fault.\", \"confidence\": 0.2}], \"summary\": \"The netlist's passive values and the zener and Q1/Q2 polarities look correct. The most likely deviation is the 74LVC1G34 buffer U4 being powered from the raw VCC input instead of the regulated +5V rail, which could exceed its voltage rating.\"}",
